55    write(22, "# iOS HIG Review \342\200\224 SampleScreen.tsx\n\nScreen type: Profile (assumed) \302\267 Primary action: \"OK\" button \302\267 Target: iPhone\n\n## Findings (per references/checklist.md)\n\n| # | Severity | Issue | RN/Expo hint |\n|---|----------|-------|--------------|\n| 1 | High | Touch target is 30x30pt, below the 44x44pt minimum. | Set `minWidth/minHeight: 44` or wrap with `hitSlop`. |\n| 2 | High | Root not scrollable; content can overflow on small devices. | Use `ScrollView`/`FlatList` with `contentInsetAdjustmentBehavior=\"automatic\"`. |\n| 3 | High | Hard-coded `paddingTop: 40` instead of safe-area insets. | Use `SafeAreaView` / `useSafeAreaInsets()`. |\n| 4 | Medium | Error state encoded by `color:'red'` alone (color-only state). | Pair with an icon/label; use `PlatformColor('systemRed')`. |\n| 5 | Medium | Hard-coded hex colors instead of semantic system colors. | Use `PlatformColor` / `DynamicColorIOS` (label, systemBackground). |\n| 6 | Medium | `fontSize: 12` error text risks poor scanability / Dynamic Type. | Use system text styles; ensure `allowFontScaling` (default true). |\n| 7 | Low | Icon/label pairing: \"OK\" button lacks accessibility label. | Add `accessibilityLabel` / `accessibilityRole=\"button\"`. |\n| 8 | Low | No loading/empty/offline states designed. | Add explicit state views per checklist \"States\". |\n\n## Summary\n8 issues: 3 High, 3 Medium, 2 Low. Largest risks are tap-target size, missing scroll container, and hard-coded safe-area padding.\n", 1454) = 1454
